abstract: >-
  A Corporate Information Statement setting out the position of Advanced
  Invasives Ltd on how Invasive Knotweeds came to be present within UK rail,
  road and canal corridors, and on the mechanisms by which they continue to
  spread along them. It tests the common claim that the railway companies
  planted Japanese Knotweed to stabilise embankments against the documentary
  record, sets out the industrial planting route that better fits the earliest
  evidence, and separates the three maintenance mechanisms that drive
  contemporary spread.
